      "writtenOn": "2025-08-06T18:01:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IMPORTANT: In the new code, the compiler may think that `best_mv` may be used uninitialized.\n\nMy analysis shows that we are protected by the check at line 3530, and the fact that `bestme` and `best_mv` are always modified at the same time. Please double check my analysis.\n\nIt may be good to initialize `best_mv` to invalid values so that if we accidentally used `best_mv` without real initialization, we will detect something is wrong.",
      "revId": "51a455fc9e17d0644c73363b8527aebb2249021d",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e52bd1de_9ee30019",
        "filename": "av1/encoder/rdopt.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 3531,
      "author": {
        "id": 3678645
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-06T21:24:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Wan-Teh, you\u0027re correct in your analysis. `bestsme` acts as a \"guard\" for checking if `best_mv` is usable or not (a stronger guarantee that includes MV values being \"valid\"). If `bestsme` is `INT_MAX`, then we know we don\u0027t care about what `best_mv` contains, because either:\n- The candidate is not valid (because neither hash search nor pixel search found any)\n- (Hypothetically) a candidate was found, but it\u0027s so incredibly expensive that it can\u0027t be used anyway\n\nIf we\u0027re worried about the compiler may think that `best_mv` may be used uninitialized, then I could initialize it to `kZeroMv`. But in practice it shouldn\u0027t be needed.",
      "parentUuid": "f6b5a97b_5d718bc8",
      "revId": "51a455fc9e17d0644c73363b8527aebb2249021d",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    }
